Source: athena-base-files
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Athena Linux <athena@local>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.0

Package: athena-base-files
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, base-files
Description: @DISTRIBUTION@ identity files (issue, motd, os-release)
 Rebrands the four user-visible identity files shipped by Debian's
 Essential base-files package so the installed system presents as
 @DISTRIBUTION@ Linux (codename @CODENAME@):
 .
   * /etc/issue            — TTY login banner
   * /etc/issue.net        — SSH/telnet login banner
   * /etc/motd             — message of the day
   * /usr/lib/os-release   — the canonical os-release file (and
                             therefore /etc/os-release, which is a
                             symlink to it on Debian)
 .
 base-files is Essential and cannot be cleanly replaced via apt
 P/C/R, so this package leaves base-files in place and uses
 dpkg-divert (preinst) to rename the four upstream files to
 *.upstream and substitute our content at the canonical paths.
 prerm reverses the diversions on package removal.
 .
 Reflected downstream:
   - gnome-control-center About panel shows "@DISTRIBUTION@ Linux"
   - The LOGO=asgard field resolves to the asgard.svg pixmap
     shipped by athena-branding
   - GRUB's lsb_release fallback returns @DISTRIBUTION@
